        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2006",
        "question_text": "<p>To bisect a given angle using a compass and straightedge, which of the following steps is <b>not</b> required?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Bisecting an angle requires drawing an arc from the vertex to intersect the angle arms, then drawing intersecting arcs from those points. <b>Drawing a perpendicular line from the vertex</b> is not part of the standard bisection procedure.</p>",
